================================================================================
Method attribution — not a code dependency
================================================================================

  TeaCache — https://github.com/ali-vilab/TeaCache

      The step-caching method used by the boogu_image transformer originates in
      the TeaCache work, and the vendored code refers to it by name. No code was
      taken from the TeaCache repository. The implementation, its TeaCacheParams
      container and its fitted rescale coefficients come from
      VectorSpaceLab/OmniGen2 (Apache-2.0, attributed above), from which
      Boogu-Image derives its transformer. TeaCache fits those coefficients per
      model architecture; this particular fit is OmniGen2's.

      Recorded so that the provenance of that polynomial does not have to be
      re-measured by the next reader.

================================================================================
First-party notice — Taylor-expansion feature cache
================================================================================

backend/app/engine/models/families/boogu_image/taylor_cache.py, together with
the re-export modules boogu_image/vendor/cache_functions and
boogu_image/vendor/taylorseer_utils, is first-party code licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

It was written clean-room from the published method in "From Reusing to
Forecasting: Accelerating Diffusion Models with TaylorSeers" (ICCV 2025) and
from Boogu-Image's own Apache-2.0 caller, by an author who had not read the
GPL-3.0-derived implementation it replaces. That implementation has been removed
from this repository in its entirety. It is therefore deliberately NOT
attributed here: nothing derived from it remains, and attributing absent code
would misstate what this software contains.
